invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_hw.c
catches: ghash_equiv_test
reason: the AES=hw one-pass seal hashes each pass's ciphertext beside the
  next pass's AES rounds and drops the hash of the last pass, which has
  no pass after it, so every tag over a record of one whole pass or more
  leaves out up to 128 bytes of ciphertext and a forger may change them.
  The ciphertext itself stays right, so only a check of the tag sees it.
  bin/ghash_equiv_test seals every payload length through three passes
  and random lengths up to 16,384 bytes on both paths and compares the
  tags byte for byte.

--- old
    ghash_hash_pass(&s.ghash, &out[(passes - 1) * GCM_HW_PASS_BYTES]);
--- new
    (void)out;
